y role), and adjust the :145 'verbatim in shape' text so it stays true after iam_s7 additionally grants the Titan ARN — a sid-only edit cannot make 'verbatim' true across diverging resource lists.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["bedrock-ci-oidc.md:130 and :239 are inside the f124 role definition (role name 'rebar-external-ci-bedrock', :228; Ticket f124, :233), a DIFFERENT role from iam_s7's Gerrit instance role",":158-159 for the f124 role: 'The region field is wildcarded; the MODEL is not. Claude only — a call to any other vendor's model is denied, which is the least-privilege oracle' — Claude-only IS a requirement for f124","Plan's rename rationale ('the existing name asserts a vendor restriction that was never a requirement and is now false') holds for iam_s7 post-Titan but is false for f124, whose restriction is deliberate",":145 'This is iam_s7.tf's aws_iam_policy_document.bedrock_converse, verbatim in shape' — after iam_s7 adds the Titan ARN at :16-17, the f124 resources at :244-246 (Claude-only) diverge in RESOURCES, so a sid-only edit leaves 'verbatim in shape' false","AC2 asserts 'its claim that the policy matches iam_s7.tf verbatim is true after the rename' — unachievable by the described sid-only edits"],"finding":"The runbook edit (Approach bullet 4 + AC2) is mechanically unsound: the sid occurrences at bedrock-ci-oidc.md:130/:239 belong to the separate f124 external-CI role, which is intentionally Claude-only, and a sid rename alone cannot make the ':145 verbatim in shape' claim true once iam_s7 gains the Titan ARN that f124 lacks.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcf956990d39f67ec","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach bullet 4; Acceptance Criteria item 2","norm_id":"n21b327ebb13cba86","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer mechanically copies iam_s7's new vendor-neutral sid onto the f124 policy, mislabeling a deliberately Claude-only role","Reviewer greps for the old sid, finds none, marks AC2 done — but the :145 'verbatim' claim is now false on resources, re-introducing exactly the stale-documentation defect the plan set out to fix"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Keep the f124 policy's own descriptive sid (or rename it to describe f124's own Claude-only grant), and rewrite :145 to 'the same shape as iam_s7.tf's bedrock_converse, which additionally grants the Titan embedding ARN', rather than requiring verbatim equality that the Titan addition breaks.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Clarify in the Approach/AC2 whether the runbook's :130/:239 sid occurrences (external-CI OIDC role) are to be renamed to the new sid or left as-is, and reconcile that with the :145 'verbatim' claim so the runbook stays accurate about the separate role.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.198,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach: 'reproduces the sid verbatim at :130 and :239 for a separate external-CI OIDC role and claims at :145 that it is iam_s7.tf's shape verbatim'","AC2: 'reproduces the current sid at every occurrence, and its claim that the policy matches iam_s7.tf verbatim is true after the rename'"],"finding":"AC2 and the Approach are slightly ambiguous about whether the runbook's old-sid occurrences at :130/:239 (which the plan says belong to a SEPARATE external-CI OIDC role) should be renamed to the new sid, or whether only the :145 'verbatim' claim is reconciled. AC2 requires the runbook to 'reproduce the current sid at every occurrence', but if the separate OIDC role's live policy still carries the old sid, rewriting :130/:239 to the new sid could misdescribe that other role.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9fde52fc404d7df6","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach bullet 4; AC2","norm_id":"n5b33b78acae8f549","priority":0.402,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor renames the runbook's :130/:239 sid for the external-CI OIDC role to match iam_s7.tf, when that role's actual deployed policy may still use the old sid, creating a new false claim."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State explicitly that the runbook reproduces iam_s7.tf's statement as the canonical shape, so :130/:239 adopt the new sid, and confirm the external-CI OIDC role's live policy shares that sid (or scope AC2 to only the :145 claim if it does not).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisi